430
00:29:37,850 --> 00:29:42,690
These measures would reduce year 2 operating costs by an estimated 10%.

431
00:29:42,690 --> 00:29:44,610
Let's quantify that recovery.

432
00:29:44,610 --> 00:29:50,250
If we implement a 10% operating cost reduction in year 2 of the pessimistic scenario, how

433
00:29:50,250 --> 00:29:53,070
does the NPV change?

434
00:29:53,070 --> 00:29:59,710
Implementing those cost controls, the NPV becomes a positive $120,000, and the IRR

435
00:29:59,710 --> 00:30:01,510
is 13.8%.

436
00:30:01,510 --> 00:30:03,070
Now we're talking.

437
00:30:03,070 --> 00:30:07,430
This provides a clear path to profitability even under adverse conditions.

438
00:30:07,430 --> 00:30:11,470
It demonstrates that the management team has a viable exit strategy.

439
00:30:11,470 --> 00:30:13,130
This is a crucial finding.

440
00:30:13,130 --> 00:30:18,030
The board will want to see that mitigating action is quantifiable and tied to specific

441
00:30:18,030 --> 00:30:19,430
performance thresholds.

442
00:30:19,430 --> 00:30:20,430
Precisely.

443
00:30:20,430 --> 00:30:23,750
Now, let's pivot to the optimistic scenario.

444
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:27,010
What happens if everything goes better than expected?

445
00:30:27,010 --> 00:30:32,830
The optimistic scenario assumes a 20% higher sales volume due to a rapid adoption rate

446
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:34,750
and minimal competitive interference.

447
00:30:34,750 --> 00:30:36,650
Good morning, Priya.

448
00:30:36,650 --> 00:30:42,530
Thanks for making time to walk through the final evaluation of these two investment projects.

449
00:30:42,530 --> 00:30:49,630
I know we both have strong perspectives, but we need to land on a unified recommendation.

450
00:30:49,630 --> 00:30:51,550
Good morning, Arjun.

451
00:30:51,550 --> 00:30:52,550
Absolutely.

452
00:30:52,550 --> 00:30:57,110
I'm keen to hear your final take on the numbers, especially after our last discussion

453
00:30:57,110 --> 00:31:03,190
on Project Alpha, the cloud inventory system, and the projected volatility.

454
00:31:03,190 --> 00:31:10,370
Right. From a purely financial standpoint, the difference is clear. Project Alpha has

455
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:17,190
a significantly higher NPV, confirming it would generate more value than Project Beta,

456
00:31:17,190 --> 00:31:19,570
the product line upgrade.

457
00:31:19,570 --> 00:31:26,370
I saw that. The larger NPV for Alpha confirms the massive potential return on investment

458
00:31:26,370 --> 00:31:32,800
