459
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:40,300
risk-adjusted return. While the expected return is higher, my sensitivity analysis flags major

460
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:47,260
concerns. Project Alpha requires substantial upfront development and a larger engineering team.

461
00:31:47,980 --> 00:31:53,500
This translates directly into a higher cost overruns and schedule delays,

462
00:31:53,500 --> 00:31:56,700
which could completely erode that NPV advantage.

463
00:31:56,700 --> 00:32:02,700
I acknowledge the higher operational risk, Arjun. We're entering a new product space,

464
00:32:02,700 --> 00:32:09,660
but I believe focusing too heavily on short-term financial safety with Project Beta would be a

465
00:32:09,660 --> 00:32:16,980
strategic mistake. Why do you view it as a mistake? Project Beta offers a guaranteed positive,

466
00:32:16,980 --> 00:32:23,940
steady cash flow and a quick launch utilizing existing resources. It's the definition of a

467
00:32:23,940 --> 00:32:26,530
a safe, profitable bet.

468
00:32:26,530 --> 00:32:29,450
Because the tech industry is pivoting hard

469
00:32:29,450 --> 00:32:32,530
toward automated cloud-based solutions.

470
00:32:32,530 --> 00:32:35,290
Project Alpha isn't just a product.

471
00:32:35,290 --> 00:32:38,210
It's a strategic positioning move.

472
00:32:38,210 --> 00:32:40,690
Being an early mover in that market segment,

473
00:32:40,690 --> 00:32:44,690
small retail, gives Nova Tech a huge competitive advantage

474
00:32:44,690 --> 00:32:46,490
for long-term growth.

475
00:32:46,490 --> 00:32:49,770
Competitive advantage at a higher cost of capital

476
00:32:49,770 --> 00:32:51,570
and higher risk.

477
00:32:51,570 --> 00:32:57,450
My forecast shows the payback period for alpha is almost twice as long as betas.

478
00:32:57,450 --> 00:33:02,580
That ties up capital for a longer duration, limiting our flexibility.

479
00:33:02,580 --> 00:33:05,580
But consider the market expansion.

480
00:33:05,580 --> 00:33:09,900
Project beta simply upgrades our current customer base.

481
00:33:09,900 --> 00:33:13,340
Alpha opens up an entirely new market segment.

482
00:33:13,340 --> 00:33:18,660
If we miss this window, a competitor will surely step in and our future competitiveness

483
00:33:18,660 --> 00:33:20,140
will suffer.

484
00:33:20,140 --> 00:33:22,820
I agree that the market is shifting.

485
00:33:22,820 --> 00:33:28,620
That's why I ran a deeper analysis on the expected cash flows under a scenario of development

486
00:33:28,620 --> 00:33:29,820
delay.

487
00:33:29,820 --> 00:33:36,260
If the alpha launch is delayed by six months, the NPV drops significantly, though it remains

488
00:33:36,260 --> 00:33:37,380
